---
import Image from "astro/components/Image.astro";

import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import auditionImage from "../assets/audition.jpg";
---

<Layout title="Audition" alt="SBSB performing on stage" img={auditionImage}>
  <div class="mx-5 mt-10 flex flex-col items-center justify-start gap-5">
    <div
      class="text-md relative flex flex-col gap-5 rounded-2xl bg-[#00000066] p-5 backdrop-blur-xl md:text-lg"
    >
      <p class="md:px-36">
        Every year, Something Borrowed Something Blue looks for new students to
        join its tight-knit family of unique voices and personalities. As a
        group, we cherish the diverse symphony of musical talent that God has
        brought to Duke for his beautiful and mysterious purposes, and we highly
        encourage both those who are well-versed in and new to a cappella to
        give auditions a try.
      </p>
      <p class="md:px-36">
        <span class="font-bold">Audition</span><br />

        <a
          class="underline"
          href="https://www.signupgenius.com/go/10C0A4CACAA23A3F8C70-65393193-sbsb#/"
          >Sign up for 2026-2027 SBSB auditions here!</a
        >
        <br /><br />
        Auditions will be held during the evenings of Monday, Aug. 31 - Thursday,
        Sept. 3 on East Campus (Biddle 086).<br /><br />
        Before your audition, stay hydrated and prepare a <span
          class="underline">verse and chorus</span
        > of any song you love. While your options are endless, choose something
        that lets you comfortably showcase your vocal range and express emotion -
        we want to meet YOU through your music.<br /><br />
        We&apos;ll also be checking your sightreading skills, ear for pitch, and
        - most importantly - your favorite candy.
      </p>
      <p class="md:px-36">
        <span class="font-bold">Questions</span><br />
        Feel free to shoot us an email at <a
          href="mailto:dukesbsb@gmail.com"
          class="underline">dukesbsb@gmail.com</a
        >. For a taste of life in SBSB, check out our Instagram!
      </p>
      <p class="md:px-36">
        The purpose of Something Borrowed Something Blue, as stated in our
        constitution, is “To glorify God through music and community.” We pray
        at the start and end of each rehearsal, sing worship music, and engage
        in discussions about the Bible and how we can best live as Jesus taught
        us, which is to love God and one another. While we welcome all to our
        group, we ask that potential new members reflect upon their own
        spirituality and whether or not they would be comfortable in this type
        of environment.
      </p>
      <p class="md:px-36">
        As a group, we are praying for wisdom and guidance for this upcoming
        year. We can't wait to see what is in store for you!
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
